# Angular client

## Structure

- `core/` — auth, i18n, API, notifications
- `features/{role|area}/` — feature components
- `shared/` — reusable UI (menus, dialogs, switchers)

## Components

- Prefer **standalone** components with `inject()` and `signal()` for UI state.
- Colocate `*.ts`, `*.html`, `*.css`.
- Use Reactive Forms (`FormBuilder.nonNullable`) for forms.
- Use `TranslatePipe` / `TranslationService` for user-facing strings — avoid hard-coded copy when i18n exists.

```typescript
@Component({ standalone: true, imports: [...], templateUrl: './login.html' })
export class LoginComponent {
  private readonly auth = inject(AuthService);
  readonly loading = signal(false);
  readonly error = signal<string | null>(null);
}
```

## API & auth

- Prefer NSwag clients from `core/api/academy-api.generated.ts` (e.g. `LessonsClient`).
- Do not hand-edit the generated file; rebuild Server after API changes.
- Auth: `AuthService`, `TokenStorageService`, `auth.interceptor`, `auth.guard` / `role.guard`.
- Realtime notifications: existing `NotificationService` + SignalR — extend, don't fork.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS 4 utility classes; match existing shell/feature layout patterns.
